WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:09.200
in this continuing, almost never ending saga of&nbsp;
trying to get covid relief passed. Joe Biden has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:17.200
negotiated not with Republicans, but with more&nbsp;
moderate Democrats to further restrict who is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:24.480
eligible for a stimulus check. What if you're&nbsp;
wondering, great, now that they've negotiated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:29.600
which Republicans are going to support the bill&nbsp;
as a result of the negotiation? The answer is, I'm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:37.920
not aware of any. This is Democrats negotiating&nbsp;
with Democrats to weaken covid stimulus just to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:44.080
get it passed. And either way, it doesn't appear&nbsp;
as though Republicans are going to support this.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:51.040
Now, I know that there are people in my audience&nbsp;
who will be mad for this critique. But come on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:55.440
guys, 2000 now, I mean, I'm going to get&nbsp;
to the pragmatic piece, so just let me&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:59.680
let me work through it. OK, here's the just&nbsp;
disgusting, frustrating part of all of this.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:04.560
Two thousand dollars became fourteen hundred. And&nbsp;
when I critique that, some people wrote to me and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:09.840
said, David, it was obvious from the beginning&nbsp;
Joe Biden meant we would add fourteen hundred to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:14.720
the six hundred to make it 2000. That's not a fair&nbsp;
critique. You're doing a bad critique, David. OK,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:19.840
then I say, well, Joe Biden said it would pass&nbsp;
right away and it didn't pass right away. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:24.480
March and I critique that. And some people wrote&nbsp;
to me and said, David, you know, you should have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:30.000
known that when a president says right away,&nbsp;
they don't mean right away. They mean months. OK,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:37.280
and now to get the fourteen hundred dollar check,&nbsp;
the checks are going to phase out more quickly as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:42.880
income goes up. So here is the changes that were&nbsp;
made under the old plan passed by the House.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:48.400
You get fourteen hundred dollars if your&nbsp;
income is up to seventy five thousand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:52.720
and it starts phasing down to zero once&nbsp;
your income is one hundred thousand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:59.920
under the new plan, it's just more restrictive.&nbsp;
The fourteen hundred starts phasing out and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:07.440
it goes to zero at 80 grand instead of at one&nbsp;
hundred grand. So in short, in the House version,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:12.720
anyone making over one hundred thousand gets&nbsp;
zero in the Senate version that was negotiated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:18.320
yesterday between Biden and Senate Republicans,&nbsp;
anyone earning over eighty thousand dollars a year&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:24.480
gets zero. Now, do I think that this is a&nbsp;
really dumb negotiation? Yes, the phase out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:30.400
at one hundred thousand dollars was fine. But the&nbsp;
reality is with a 50 50 majority in the Senate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:36.560
50/50 with Comilla, as the deciding vote enties,&nbsp;
Democrats can't afford to lose a single vote.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:42.640
So Joe Manchin now has power. Jeanne Shaheen,&nbsp;
a Democrat from New Hampshire who also wanted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:49.840
to restrict the checks. She has power. She wants&nbsp;
to take the money saved by dropping the limit and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:57.040
send that money to hospitals. OK, does it still&nbsp;
make sense to pass this bill? It does. In addition&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:01.600
to the stimulus checks, the bill has three&nbsp;
hundred and fifty billion dollars for states.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:05.840
One hundred and thirty billion dollars for opening&nbsp;
schools. One hundred and sixty billion dollars for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:11.920
vaccinations and tax testing and enhanced child&nbsp;
tax credit rental assistance, food assistance. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:17.440
it's important to pass this regardless and&nbsp;
we can't keep delaying it. But is this a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:22.320
really lame negotiation where it's Democrats&nbsp;
negotiating with Democrats and either way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:26.480
Republicans won't support it? Of course&nbsp;
it is. At some point we have to recognize,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:31.840
even though there are Democrats there, they're&nbsp;
very moderate. Some, we would even say are almost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:38.080
sort of like centrist Republicans, people like&nbsp;
Joe Manchin. It's just the reality. And it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:42.320
not even that. I think it's that important that&nbsp;
people earning ninety eight thousand dollars get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:48.000
a check. Like it's more the idea that we have&nbsp;
zero Republicans on board. It's an emergency to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.560
pass this. And Democrats are negotiating&nbsp;
with each other over whether the cutoff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:56.400
should be 80 grand or 100 grand. It's sort of&nbsp;
like a what are we doing here type of moment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.400 --> 00:04:01.200
I get that if you make ninety eight thousand&nbsp;
dollars, you make fourteen hundred bucks and like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:08.400
five or six days of work. This is less about that.&nbsp;
It's the big picture of absurdity of how it hasn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:13.520
even nearly been only because of Republicans&nbsp;
that this hasn't passed. And of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:18.160
the 15 dollar minimum wage is just gone from the&nbsp;
bill altogether. But we've already covered that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:23.920
and we knew it now on the on the minimum wage.&nbsp;
I'm getting some emails, which I support. OK,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:28.480
I'm getting emails from people saying, David, you&nbsp;
know, the Senate parliamentarian who decided you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:35.200
can't do the 15 dollar minimum wage in this bill.&nbsp;
The Senate parliamentarian can just be overruled.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:39.120
It's not you know, people are acting like,&nbsp;
oh, it would be a massive step to overrule&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:44.400
the Senate parliamentarian. OK, yeah, it would&nbsp;
or it wouldn't. But the truth is, if you overrule&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:50.080
the Senate parliamentarian and you include a 15&nbsp;
dollar minimum wage in the covid relief bill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:54.880
I just don't think it passes. I don't think Joe&nbsp;
Manchin votes for the bill. And you can't afford&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:59.520
to lose a single vote in the Senate right now,&nbsp;
given that no Republicans plan to vote for it. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:05.280
I'm just as disgusted as you are by what's going&nbsp;
on. Don't don't mistake this for me, not being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:11.600
disgusted in a practical reality. They're just&nbsp;
not going to vote for it. If it's in the bill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:15.840
it's not going to pass, even if you override the&nbsp;
Senate parliamentarian and put it in the bill.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:20.320
It's not going to get passed. Now, you could make&nbsp;
the argument and I know some in my audience will,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:25.760
that it's worth it and it's worth it. Not passing&nbsp;
to get those Democratic senators on the record&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:28.560
saying they're against it. They're already&nbsp;
on the record. They've said it in interviews.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:33.440
They've they've put statements out. So you're&nbsp;
just slowing down, getting money to anybody.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:40.000
And but bottom line is, we've been&nbsp;
talking about since November 4th,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:45.360
even with the two Georgia Senate seats&nbsp;
that Democrats took from Republicans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:51.120
you still need to convince Joe Manchin that wasn't&nbsp;
an understatement. That wasn't just something I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:56.640
said for fun. It's Joe Manchin and it's Jeanne&nbsp;
Shaheen. And over the next couple of years, it'll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.640 --> 00:06:01.760
be one or two other Democratic senators as well.&nbsp;
The answer is we have to flip more seats saying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:08.560
primary. Joe Manchin in West Virginia. If you run&nbsp;
Bernie in West Virginia against Joe Manchin and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:16.480
somehow Bernie wins the primary, then a Republican&nbsp;
